      "worked": "Let $L$ be the lighthouse. A bearings sketch gives $\\angle ALB=20^\\circ+40^\\circ=60^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=7^2+12^2-2(7)(12)\\cos60^\\circ\\\\AB^2&=109\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{109}\\text{ km}\\\\AB&\\approx10.4\\text{ km}\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$\n\nLet $\\alpha=\\angle LAB$. Use the exact length $AB=\\sqrt{109}$ in the cosine rule.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac{7^2+(\\sqrt{109})^2-12^2}{2(7)\\sqrt{109}}\\\\\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{109}}\\\\\\alpha&=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{109}}\\right)\\\\\\alpha&\\approx84.503633455^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bearing of $L$ from $A$ is $20^\\circ+180^\\circ=200^\\circ$. Ship $B$ lies clockwise from $AL$. Let its bearing from $A$ be $b$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=200^\\circ+\\alpha\\\\b&\\approx284.503633455^\\circ\\\\b&\\approx285^\\circ\\quad\\text{(nearest degree)}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
